Origin: or מִכְמֹר; from 3648 in the sense of blackening by heat;
Meaning: a (hunter's) net (as dark from concealment)
KJV renders: net.

H4365.strongs:
Origin: or מִכְמֹרֶת; feminine of 4364;
Meaning: a (fisher's) net
KJV renders: drag, net.

H4366.strongs:
Origin: apparently from an unused root meaning to hide; concealment;
Meaning: Mikmethath, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Michmethath.

H4367.strongs:
Origin: from 4100 and 5068 with a particle interposed; what (is) like (a) liberal (man) ?;
Meaning: Maknadbai, an Israelite
KJV renders: Machnadebai.

H4368.strongs:
Origin: the same as 4350; a base;
Meaning: Mekonah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Mekonah.

H4369.strongs:
Origin: the same as 4350;
Meaning: a spot
KJV renders: base.

H4370.strongs:
Origin: from 3647 in the sense of hiding;
Meaning: (only in dual) drawers (from concealing the private parts)
KJV renders: breeches.

H4371.strongs:
Origin: probably from an unused root meaning to enumerate;
Meaning: an assessment (as based upon a census)
KJV renders: tribute.

H4372.strongs:
Origin: from 3680;
Meaning: a covering, i.e. weatherboarding
KJV renders: covering.

H4373.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4371;
Meaning: an enumeration; by implication, a valuation
KJV renders: number, worth.

H4374.strongs:
Origin: from 3680;
Meaning: a covering, i.e. garment; specifically, a coverlet (for a bed), an awning (from the sun); also the omentum (as covering the intestines)
KJV renders: clothing, to cover, that which covereth.

H4375.strongs:
Origin: from 3717; a fold;
Meaning: Makpelah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Machpelah.

H4376.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to sell, literally (as merchandise, a daughter in marriage, into slavery), or figuratively (to surrender)
KJV renders: × at all, sell (away, -er, self).

H4377.strongs:
Origin: from 4376;
Meaning: merchandise; also value
KJV renders: pay, price, ware.

H4378.strongs:
Origin: from 5234;
Meaning: an acquaintance
KJV renders: acquaintance.

H4379.strongs:
Origin: from 3738;
Meaning: a pit (for salt)
KJV renders: (salt-) pit.

H4380.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 3564 in the sense of stabbing;
Meaning: a sword
KJV renders: habitation.

H4381.strongs:
Origin: from 4376; salesman;
Meaning: Mikri, an Israelite
KJV renders: Michri.

H4382.strongs:
Origin: patrial from an unused name (the same as 4380) of a place in Palestine;
Meaning: a Mekerathite, or inhabitant of Mekerah
KJV renders: Mecherathite.

H4383.strongs:
Origin: or מִכְשֹׁל; masculine from 3782;
Meaning: a stumbling-block, literally or figuratively (obstacle, enticement (specifically an idol), scruple)
KJV renders: caused to fall, offence, × (no-) thing offered, ruin, stumbling-block.

H4384.strongs:
Origin: feminine from 3782;
Meaning: a stumbling-block, but only figuratively (fall, enticement [idol])
KJV renders: ruin, stumbling-block.

H4385.strongs:
Origin: from 3789;
Meaning: a thing written, the characters, or a document (letter, copy, edict, poem)
KJV renders: writing.

H4386.strongs:
Origin: from 3807;
Meaning: a fracture
KJV renders: bursting.

H4387.strongs:
Origin: from 3799;
Meaning: an engraving, i.e. (techn.) a poem
KJV renders: Michtam.

H4388.strongs:
Origin: from 3806;
Meaning: a mortar; by analogy, a socket (of a tooth)
KJV renders: hollow place, mortar.

H4389.strongs:
Origin: the same as 4388;
Meaning: dell; the Maktesh, a place in Jerusalem
KJV renders: Maktesh.

H4390.strongs:
Origin: or מָלָא; (Esther 7:5), a primitive root;
Meaning: to fill or (intransitively) be full of, in a wide application (literally and figuratively)
KJV renders: accomplish, confirm, consecrate, be at an end, be expired, be fenced, fill, fulfil, (be, become, × draw, give in, go) full(-ly, -ly set, tale), (over-) flow, fulness, furnish, gather (selves, together), presume, replenish, satisfy, set, space, take a (hand-) full, have wholly.

H4391.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 4390;
Meaning: to fill
KJV renders: fill, be full.

H4392.strongs:
Origin: from 4390;
Meaning: full (literally or figuratively) or filling (literally); also (concretely) fulness; adverbially, fully
KJV renders: × she that was with child, fill(-ed, -ed with), full(-ly), multitude, as is worth.

H4393.strongs:
Origin: rarely מְלוֹא; or מְלוֹ; (Ezekiel 41:8), from 4390;
Meaning: fulness (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: × all along, × all that is (there-) in, fill, (× that whereof...was) full, fulness, (hand-) full, multitude.

H4394.strongs:
Origin: from 4390;
Meaning: a fulfilling (only in plural), i.e. (literally) a setting (of gems), or (technically) consecration (also concretely, a dedicatory sacrifice)
KJV renders: consecration, be set.

H4395.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4392;
Meaning: something fulfilled, i.e. abundance (of produce)
KJV renders: (first of ripe) fruit, fulness.

H4396.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 4394;
Meaning: a filling, i.e. setting (of gems)
KJV renders: enclosing, setting.

H4397.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to despatch as a deputy;
Meaning: a messenger; specifically, of God, i.e. an angel (also a prophet, priest or teacher)
KJV renders: ambassador, angel, king, messenger.

H4398.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 4397;
Meaning: an angel
KJV renders: angel.

H4399.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 4397;
Meaning: properly, deputyship, i.e. ministry; generally, employment (never servile) or work (abstractly or concretely); also property (as the result of labor)
KJV renders: business, cattle, industrious, occupation, ( -pied), officer, thing (made), use, (manner of) work((-man), -manship).
